  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Application Scope**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core requirements for this AI-powered file sorting application. Focusing on the user\'s need for a universal, cross-platform desktop application that runs natively on macOS, Windows, and Linux from a single codebase. I\'m starting with the initial parameters.\n\n\n**Analyzing AI Integration Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the AI integration, focusing on the Ollama connection and model selection. The app will use an Ollama instance, configurable via settings, and a dropdown for model selection sourced from `/api/tags`. I\'m outlining how the file content is analyzed, handling both text-based files and other formats using filename, extension, size, metadata, and optional vision model analysis. I\'m exploring API options to connect to the LLM.\n\n\n**Designing the Interface**\n\nI\'m now deep in interface design, particularly the \"Watch Tab.\" I\'m thinking about live statistics displays: files sorted, queue depth, and decision time. Real-time folder status indicators are important too. A live queue with file analysis status, confidence, reasoning, and review controls is my next focus. I\'m also planning a Decision Engine console with timestamps and tags, and a simulation/upload feature for testing.\n\n\n**Developing the Core Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial features like drag-and-drop file support. I\'m focusing on the \"Shelf Tab,\" with its hierarchical display of target folders and sorted files, offering interactive views, search functionality, and file actions. The \"Rules Tab\" is being designed for rule creation, editing, and deletion, including source and target folder specifications, rule categories, and system prompt editing. I\'m also planning the \"Activity Tab\" as a chronological log of all sorting events.\n\n\n**Refining Action Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now implementing undo functionality, focusing on per-entry and bulk undo options, enabling file reversions. I\'m building filters for the activity log, including \"All,\" \"Sorted,\" \"Arrivals,\" \"Skipped,\" \"System,\" and \"Errors,\" and incorporating CSV export. I\'m also planning the Settings Tab with Ollama connection details, including fallback options for the Gemini API key and Watch Behavior. I\'m exploring persistent database options (SQLite/IndexedDB/JSON) and simulating OS-native permission triggers. I am designing file operation rules around move actions and handling duplicate filenames.\n\n\n**Implementing File Handling**\n\nI\'m now focused on robust file handling. I\'m building in an append-incrementing counter for duplicate filenames, handling locked or in-use files by skipping them and logging a warning with a retry next cycle. I\'m also planning large file support, up to 4 GB, using streaming to avoid main thread locking. Logging failed sorts with the exact reason and maintaining an undo journal for full state tracking are also in progress.\n\n\n**Refining Frontend & Backend**\n\nI\'m now implementing the user interface with React, Tailwind CSS, Lucide icons, and Motion for state transitions, targeting fast responsiveness. I\'m focusing on the backend and following full-stack application guidelines (Express + Vite). I\'m refining the `package.json` scripts and implementing the `server.ts` file to bind to port 3000 and 0.0.0.0. I\'m also implementing the Express server to proxy Ollama requests and handle the Gemini API requests using the `@google/genai` package, as well as handle the local File System API for folder operations.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 166355312
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
