  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Application Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the application\'s architecture and the key components. Specifically, I\'m fleshing out the backend\'s role, including the Ollama proxy API, responsible for interfacing with local Ollama endpoints. The server modules are also under consideration, which will organize the various services.\n\n\n**Outlining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m currently detailing the API endpoints. I\'ve defined `/api/ollama/` for interacting with Ollama, including tags and chat functionalities. `/api/gemini/classify` handles Gemini-based AI, and I am also working on endpoints for file system and database management, with virtual and physical storage paths. I\'m focusing on the configuration directory and watch/target shelf folders, as well as file operations like listing and content extraction.\n\n\n**Detailing File Management System**\n\nI\'m now detailing the file management system\'s API. I\'m focusing on `/api/fs/upload` for file uploads, including `.txt`, `.md`, and other formats up to size limits. Duplicate handling is key: I\'m implementing incrementing counters for duplicate filenames. I\'m also addressing locked file scenarios, implementing a simulated locked file detection system. Furthermore, I\'m working on the `sift-db.json` persistence, using a reversible undo journal for all file movements.\n\n\n**Defining Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the frontend (`src/*`). I\'ve defined TypeScript types, including `Rule`, `Category`, `SortingFile`, and others. In the `TopBar`, I\'m including model selection, mode toggles, status indicators, and platform controls. The `SidebarNav` will feature tabs for various views, and the `WatchView` will include stats, folder bars, file cards with real-time status and actions. I\'m also including a decision engine console with streaming logs, and the data will persist across reloads and restarts, auto reloading on boot.\n\n\n**Designing User Interface Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the application\'s user interface components. I am designing several key views, like `ShelfView`, with a target folders grid. I\'m focusing on features such as folder colors, file list tables with detailed metadata, and undo buttons. The `RulesView` will have a multi-rule manager, while an `ActivityView` will include a chronological log with filtering options and undo functionalities. I am also working on drag-and-drop file upload, and clear console.\n\n\n**Defining Settings Interface**\n\nI am now focusing on the settings interface, which will allow users to configure Ollama connections, set Gemini fallback parameters, and adjust watch behavior. There will also be a section to manage OS permissions and reset database and storage. Finally, I will create an OS permission dialog mockup.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 29
      nanos: 40177544
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
