  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on creating modular UI components. Specifically, I\'m starting with `src/components/TopBar.tsx`. This includes the application title \"Sift,\" a version badge, and a platform selector toggle. I\'m also building an Ollama model dropdown and segmented controls for Auto-Sort and Review modes, for efficient interaction.\n\n\n**Expanding the UI Framework**\n\nI\'ve moved on from the TopBar to flesh out `src/components/Sidebar.tsx`. I\'m designing nav items for each tab: Watch, Shelf, Rules, Activity, and Settings, and including an Engine Status Card. Next, I\'ll tackle `src/components/WatchView.tsx`, which involves several interactive components like statistics grids and real-time status displays. I\'m focusing on user interaction and dynamic data visualization now.\n\n\n**Defining Shelf & Rules**\n\nI\'m now diving into the Shelf and Rules views. For the shelf, I\'m envisioning an interactive Target Folders Grid with category cards and dynamic file list tables. The Rules view focuses on a rule editor with folder mapping, a category list editor, a system prompt template, and a test rule simulator. I\'m prioritizing user control and clarity in these designs.\n\n\n**Designing the Activity View**\n\nI\'m now detailing the Activity View with these columns: Time, Event type, File details, Source and Destination, Category, Engine, Confidence, Duration, and an Undo button. I\'m also adding a Bulk Undo option and a CSV export.\n\n**Building Settings and Permissions**\n\nNow, I\'m working on the Settings view, which has sections for the Ollama connection, Gemini API status, Watcher behavior, and Cross-Platform Permissions. I\'m planning an interactive Permission Modal too, for OS-level access.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 109063598
    }
