  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Summarizing Work Progress**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the build is clean and verification is complete! I\'m now focusing on a clear summary for you, highlighting key implementations. Specifically, I\'m working on detailing the Universal Cross-Platform Desktop UI aspects. I\'m focusing on crafting a concise overview for you, starting with that core component.\n\n\n**Detailing Feature Implementation**\n\nI\'ve made significant headway integrating the platform switcher for macOS, Windows, and Linux window chrome. I\'ve also implemented elegant dark/light desktop typography using Bricolage Grotesque, Instrument Sans, and JetBrains Mono. Furthermore, I\'ve integrated AI, including Ollama HTTP API connectivity, Gemini 2.5 Flash AI, and a local pattern-matching heuristic engine for offline classification. A persistent top bar with a model selector is now in place. Finally, I\'ve completed work on the Watch and Shelf tabs.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the development of **Sift** \342\200\224 a universal, cross-platform AI-powered desktop file sorting application:\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n\n- **Desktop Experience & Cross-Platform UI**:\n  - **Native OS Platform Switcher**: Toggle between macOS (security-scoped bookmarks & traffic lights), Windows (AppData permissions), and Linux (XDG config) window chromes and permission models.\n  - **Aesthetic Pairings**: Styled with *Bricolage Grotesque* display typography, *Instrument Sans* body, and *JetBrains Mono* for decision console outputs.\n\n- **AI Integration**:\n  - **Ollama HTTP API**: Connects directly to local Ollama instances (`http://localhost:11434`) via server proxy endpoints with dynamic model enumeration (`llama3.2`, `mistral`, `phi3.5`, `qwen2.5`, `gemma2`).\n  - **Gemini AI Fallback**: Integrates server-side Gemini 2.5 Flash AI as a fallback or primary classification engine.\n  - **Local Heuristics Engine**: Instant client/server pattern matching for offline execution.\n  - **Persistent Top Bar**: Model selection dropdown, **Auto-Sort** vs. **Review Mode** toggle, file drop triggers, and simulation controls.\n\n- **Tabbed Desktop Interface**:\n  - **Watch Tab**: Live stats cards (*Files sorted*, *In queue*, *Avg decision ms*, *Tokens used*), Inbox file queue with confidence meters, manual **Approve/Skip** buttons in Review mode, real-time **Decision Engine Console**, and recent decisions rail.\n  - **Shelf Tab**: Target folders grid with item count badges, category subfolders, file preview modal, and **Undo Sort** buttons.\n  - **Rules Tab**: Source Folder \342\236\224 Target Folder mapping, taxonomy category editor (colors, AI descriptions, extensions, keywords, subfolder names), and System Prompt template editor with `{categories}` tag interpolation.\n  - **Activity Tab**: Filterable chronological log table, CSV export, single-item **Undo**, and **Bulk Undo** restoration.\n  - **Settings Tab**: Ollama endpoint URL, temperature slider, timeout controls, Gemini API status, watcher pace sliders, and OS permissions manager.\n\n- **File Operations & Persistence**:\n  - Real file moves to target subfolders with duplicate filename counter resolution (`report (1).pdf`).\n  - Reversible **Undo Journal** tracking every move and allowing restoration back to the watch directory.\n  - Persistent storage in server disk database (`sift-db.json`)."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 457375482
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
